Third-party material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Standard font metrics (stdfont_metrics.go)

  The generated file stdfont_metrics.go contains advance widths for the twelve
  text fonts built into every PDF viewer (Helvetica, Times and Courier, in
  their four styles each). These are numeric metrics -- factual measurements
  required by the PDF format in order to lay out text in fonts the viewer
  supplies -- and were generated from AFM metric files distributed with the URW
  base35 font set, which are metrically compatible with Adobe's originals.

  No font outlines, font programs or font software are included in or
  distributed with this package.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fonts you embed yourself
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  This package embeds no fonts. When you call AddTTFFont or AddTTFFontData, the
  font file you supply is copied into the PDF you generate.

  Embedding a font is a form of redistribution. It is your responsibility to
  confirm that the font's license permits it. Most open fonts do, and some
  state conditions; many commercial fonts restrict or forbid embedding.
  DejaVu, Liberation, Noto and the Google Fonts collection are all safe
  choices, and are what the examples use.
